# Jaguar XJ (X351) four-door saloon, 2010-2019.
#
# The long, low XJ: a large oval mesh grille, narrow swept headlamps wrapping
# into the wings, a body-colour roof panel running back between the C-pillars,
# and slim horizontal tail lamps wrapping onto the rear wings. The standard
# wheelbase is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_XJ_(X351)
#
# Dimensions 5.130 x 1.899 x 1.461 m, wheelbase 3.032 m (standard wheelbase;
# the XJL is 5.255 m on 3.157 m).
#
# Shape reference: no true level side elevation exists in the pack. The side
# image is a front three-quarter about 30 degrees off the centre line; it is a
# standard-wheelbase 2010 car while the front and rear images are a
# long-wheelbase 2018 XJL, so the tail is reconciled to the standard car.
# No detail close-up was available. Both limitations are recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the 2014 model year UK Specification and Price Guide,
# confirmed by the 2013/14 and 2017 UK brochures. Ebony, Polaris White,
# Rhodium Silver and British Racing Green are UK brochure names. Weights 11,
# 10, 10, 9, total 40, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 250 km/h. Comfort 145/548, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 145. Classes 3,4.
# Dates 2010-2019 production, road tail staggered 2034-2037.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-xj-x351.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-xj-x351.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-xj-x351/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: no true side elevation exists; the side image is a front
# three-quarter about 30 degrees off, and it is a standard-wheelbase 2010 car
# while the front and rear images are a long-wheelbase 2018 XJL. The tail was
# reconciled to the standard car. No detail close-up was available. The tall
# J-shaped rear lamps follow the photographs; grille and lamp internals are
# simplified at sprite scale.


